<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<osis xmlns="http://www.bibletechnologies.net/2003/OSIS/namespace" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.bibletechnologies.net/2003/OSIS/namespace http://www.bibletechnologies.net/osisCore.2.1.1.xsd">
  <osisText osisIDWork="JOH_Ebr530_Translation" osisRefWork="bible" xml:lang="en">
    <header>
      <work osisWork="JOH_Ebr530_Translation">
        <title>English Translation of John (Vatican Biblioteca Apostolica ebr. 530)</title>
        <identifier type="OSIS">JOH_Ebr530_Translation</identifier>
        <scope>JOH</scope>
        <language>en</language>
        <type type="x-translation">Translation</type>
        <identifier type="shelfmark">Biblioteca Apostolica Vaticana, ebr. 530, part 1, fragment 11, folios 1r–2v</identifier>
        <contributor role="trl" file-as="Gordon, Nehemia">Nehemia Gordon</contributor>
        <date event="eversion" type="ISO">2018</date>
        <rights>© 2018 Nehemia Gordon. All rights reserved.</rights>
        <description>Hebrew transcription and English translation of John from Biblioteca Apostolica Vaticana ebr. 530, part 1, fragment 11, folios 1r–2v, a manuscript held by the Vatican Library. Transcribed, translated, and annotated by Nehemia Gordon.</description>
      </work>
      <work osisWork="bible">
        <identifier type="OSIS">bible</identifier>
        <refSystem>StandardV11N</refSystem>
        <language>en</language>
      </work>
    </header>
    <div type="book" osisID="John">
      <chapter osisID="John.1">
        <verse osisID="John.1.1" n="1">In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was next to Elohim And Elohim, he was the</verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.2" n="2">Word. (2) This was in the beginning next to</verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.3" n="3">Elohim. (3) All things were made through him and without him nothing was made<note type="footnote" n="16">The form וּשֲׂﬠַנ is found in Mishnah, Yoma 3:10 in the Kaufmann manuscript.</note> <note type="footnote" n="17">A Patach is expected in the Bet.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.4" n="4">from all that was. (4) In him was life. And life was the light</verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.5" n="5">of men. (5) And the light was shining forth in the darkness and the darkness<note type="footnote" n="18">Furtive Patach is missing under Chet.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.6" n="6">could not contain it. (6) And there was a certain man sent from God</verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.7" n="7">and his name was Yochanan. (7) This one came in testimony, to testify concerning the light in order that they would believe</verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.8" n="8">everything because of him. He was not the light, but only</verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.9" n="9">testifying concerning the light. (9) It was true light, to shed light on all to every man who enters</verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.10" n="10">into This World. (10) He was in the world and the world was made<note type="footnote" n="19">Sin dot omitted.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.11" n="11">through him. And the world did not recognize him. (11) He came to his true homeland and the children of his<note type="footnote" n="20">Cholam omitted.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.12" n="12">house did not accept him. And to all those who accepted him and believe in his name, he gave<note type="footnote" n="21">Shin dot omitted.</note> </verse>
        <verse osisID="John.1.13" n="13">dominion that they would be Sons of Elohim. (13) For they were not born out of blood and not out of the desire of the flesh and not out of the desire of men, but from<note type="footnote" n="22">Shin dot omitted.</note> </verse>
      </chapter>
    </div>
  </osisText>
</osis>
